1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,171
Here's BobHead: a big-head version of your clip, keeping the movement and original

2
00:00:06,171 --> 00:00:06,619
dialogue.

3
00:00:07,642 --> 00:00:11,923
Open BobHead on GitHub and go to Releases.

4
00:00:11,923 --> 00:00:15,135
Under Assets, download Start-BobHead dot cmd.

5
00:00:16,142 --> 00:00:20,212
Put that file in an empty folder and double-click it.

6
00:00:20,212 --> 00:00:24,690
It downloads the app, starts the engine, and opens your browser.

7
00:00:25,725 --> 00:00:30,473
Python, ComfyUI, custom nodes, and the workflow are included.

8
00:00:30,473 --> 00:00:32,583
Keep the folder together.

9
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,678
On first launch, click Download Required Models.

10
00:00:37,678 --> 00:00:41,755
Allow about 102 gigabytes, plus extra space.

11
00:00:41,755 --> 00:00:44,668
You can pause and resume.

12
00:00:45,683 --> 00:00:51,931
Mine are already installed. Once all twelve say Installed, close this window.

13
00:00:51,931 --> 00:00:56,096
Supporting models may download during your first generation.

14
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,252
Drop in a talking clip, or click to choose one.

15
00:01:01,252 --> 00:01:05,403
This example uses my own footage, with its original sound.

16
00:01:11,433 --> 00:01:16,986
Choose five seconds to start. The head effect is already set, so there's

17
00:01:16,986 --> 00:01:19,122
no size slider to adjust.

18
00:01:20,142 --> 00:01:25,199
Click Make Me a BobHead. The first frame guides the look, and the

19
00:01:25,199 --> 00:01:26,755
video guides the movement.

20
00:01:27,767 --> 00:01:31,311
This run took about four minutes on my GPU.

21
00:01:31,311 --> 00:01:33,280
I've skipped the wait here.

22
00:01:34,308 --> 00:01:37,349
Here's the result with the original dialogue.

23
00:01:37,349 --> 00:01:41,692
Play it back, then click Download MP4 to save it.

24
00:01:47,558 --> 00:01:53,216
Click Replace to try another clip. The before and after files are on

25
00:01:53,216 --> 00:01:54,087
GitHub, too.
